This page continues the 'Mesures spectrales et réarrangement de fonctions' notes. The setting is a measure space (M,m) and a measurable f. Its 'spectral measure' μ_f = f(m) is what we now call the distribution of f, viewed as a measure on C^*.

(i) End of Prop. 1. A positive decreasing φ on R^+_* is recovered from its spectral measure μ by t = ∫_{φ(t)}^∞ dμ(s), i.e. t = μ([φ(t),∞[) = m{φ ≥ φ(t)}. This holds except at the countably many ambiguous t (jumps/flat parts). So φ is the generalized inverse of the tail function s ↦ ∫_s^∞ dμ.

(ii) Proposition. A positive measurable f on M is 'spectrally equivalent' (equimeasurable) to a decreasing φ on R^+_* iff every level set f^{-1}([a,∞[), a>0, has finite measure. φ is then unique a.e. Grothendieck calls it the 'réarrangée décroissante' φ_f, today the decreasing rearrangement f^*. Two such f, g (possibly on different spaces) are equimeasurable iff φ_f = φ_g.

(iii) Variational formula (4): φ_f(t) = inf{ ||(1−E) f||_∞ : m(E) ≤ t } (resp. m(E) < t), identifying E with its indicator. This is exactly the form later used for generalized singular values of τ-measurable operators: μ_t(T) = inf{ ||T E|| : τ(1−E) ≤ t } (Fack–Kosaki).

(v) Consequences listed (5):
- monotonicity: f ≤ g ⇒ φ_f ≤ φ_g;
- homogeneity: φ_{λf} = λ φ_f;
- powers: φ_{f^α} = (φ_f)^α;
- 'subadditivity' φ_{f+g} ≤ φ_f + φ_g;
- 'submultiplicativity' φ_{fg} ≤ φ_f φ_g;
- existence statements for φ_{λf}, φ_{f+g}, φ_{fg}.

(vi) Boxed margin notes:
- ∫ f dm = ∫ s dμ_f(s) = ∫ φ_f dt, so N_p(f) = N_p(φ_f);
- more generally, for increasing α on R^+, φ_{α(f)} = α(φ_f), hence ∫ α(f) = ∫ α(φ_f).

Purpose: the next page introduces Φ_f(t) = ∫_0^t φ_f, Ψ_f = ∫_0^t log φ_f, and Δ_f = exp Ψ_{|f|}. It then derives Ψ_{fg} ≤ Ψ_f + Ψ_g, i.e. Δ_{fg} ≤ Δ_f Δ_g. These are commutative models of the Weyl/Ky Fan/Horn majorization inequalities for singular values. They are a preparation for rearrangement in von Neumann algebras with trace and for Fredholm-determinant estimates. That programme appeared as Grothendieck's Séminaire Bourbaki exposé 113 (1955), 'Réarrangements de fonctions et inégalités de convexité dans les algèbres de von Neumann munies d'une trace'.
